kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Discussion","type":"heading","anchor":"discussion","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Each entry is a step: its instrument holds until the next entry. So reversing mirrors the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"stretch each selected entry governs — up to the next selected entry, or to the range’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"upper bound — and moves the entry to that stretch’s new start. Flute at 0 and piccolo at","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"4, reversed within 0…8, gives piccolo at 0 and flute at 4. The stretch before the first","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"selected entry, which holds the instrument in effect before it (","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorModel\/documentation\/IvorModel\/InstrumentTable\/defaultInstrument","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"unless an unselected entry precedes it), moves to the end of the range, and a new entry","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"begins it there. Entries that share a time swap order, so a step keeps its order. The","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"instrument after the range isn’t restored, just as the interpolating maps don’t restore","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"their values after it.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"aside","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorModel\/documentation\/IvorModel\/InstrumentTable\/Error\/invalidAnchor","type":"reference"},{"text":" if ","type":"text"},{"code":"timeRange","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" does not contain the time","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"range of the entries being reversed; otherwise,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorModel\/documentation\/IvorModel\/InstrumentTable\/Error\/reverseFailure(_:)","type":"ref